            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Find the size of the largest angle in a triangle with side lengths 10 cm, 15 cm and 19 cm. Give your answer correct to the nearest degree.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$97^\\circ$; the largest angle is opposite the 19 cm side.",
      "worked": "The largest angle $\\theta$ is opposite the longest side, 19 cm.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{10^2+15^2-19^2}{2(10)(15)}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-0.12\\\\\\theta&\\approx96.8921^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe largest angle is $97^\\circ$, correct to the nearest degree.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
